course: dictionary
lesson: 602
title: Award: a prize and a decision
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An award is a prize or reward given for doing something well. «The Grammy Awards are voted on by members of the Recording Academy, people who work in music, not by fans.» The clues are voted on and people who work in music: an award is decided by people who judge, not by just anyone.
explain: As a verb, to award means to give a prize, money or a mark officially. «2 marks awarded for each correct answer» tells you the teacher gives marks for every right answer. Check it by swapping in given: «2 marks given for each correct answer» still makes sense, so awarded means given.
explain: Sport uses the word too. «A referee awards a penalty» means the referee officially gives a penalty. The same word can be a noun (an award) or a verb (to award), so look at the rest of the sentence to see which one it is.
fact: Award can be a noun (an award) or a verb (to award, awards, awarded, awarding).
fact: «Award» as a noun means a prize or a reward for doing something well.
fact: «Award» as a verb means to give someone a prize, money or a mark officially.
fact: In sport, a referee can award a penalty or a free kick.
fact: «Award-winning» means having won a prize for something good.
exercise: In «it won major awards», what does awards mean? | A kind of computer | A fan who votes | *A prizes given for doing something well | A small bedroom at home
exercise: «2 marks awarded for each correct answer.» What does awarded mean here? | Taken away | *Given officially | Written in pencil | Lost
exercise: «A referee awards a penalty.» What does awards mean here? | Refuses to watch | Runs after | *Officially gives | Forgets
test: «The Grammy Awards are voted on by members of the Recording Academy.» Who votes for the Grammy Awards? | Referees in sport | Fans | *Members of the Recording Academy | Teachers at a school
test: «Award-winning» means which of these? | *Having won a prize for something good | Sent off in sport | Very cheap to buy | Losing a game badly
exam: Which sentence uses award as a verb? | *The teacher will award a certificate to the best reader | Her award is on the shelf | The award ceremony is in the hall tonight | Awards are shown on the screen
